            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for a throne, then the Kannada for a crown."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಅಪರಾಧ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಪರಾಧ — aparādha — \"a crime; an offence\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಪರಾಧ ಮಾಡಿದರೆ ಶಿಕ್ಷೆ ಸಿಗುತ್ತದೆ. aparādha māḍidare śikṣe siguttade. If you commit a crime, you get punished."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One who commits a crime is an ಅಪರಾಧಿ, a criminal. A crime is \"done\": ಅಪರಾಧ (aparādha) ಮಾಡು."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಪರಾಧ (aparādha) is borrowed from Sanskrit aparādha, \"an offence, a fault\" (CDIAL 439)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
            }
          ]
        },
